Implementing the Linux cp Command Using System Calls.

Explanation:

Function - Purpose
open() - Opens or creates a file.
read() - Reads data from the source file.
write() - Writes data into the destination file.
close() - Closes the opened file.
perror() - Displays an error message.


Important concepts:

O_RDONLY – Opens a file in read-only mode.
O_WRONLY – Opens a file in write-only mode.
O_CREAT – Creates a file if it doesn't exist.
O_TRUNC – Removes existing destination content.
0644 – Sets file permissions.
buffer[1024] – Temporarily stores data while copying.
